<title>HONG KONG: Shenzhen bourse suspends two A share firms.</title>
<headline>Shenzhen bourse suspends two A share firms.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Shenzhen stock exchange has suspended two A share companies following sharp price fluctuations, exchange officials and traders said on Friday.  </p>
<p>The Shenzhen stock exchange said in a statement that trading in Shenzhen Energy Investment Co Ltd and Luzhou Old Cellar Co Ltd was suspended in the afternoon.</p>
<p>The exchange said it had summoned the top five holders of the publically-listed shares of the two companies to explain the price movements.</p>
<p>An official with Shenzhen Energy said the company had not been ramping their own shares.</p>
</text>
